			<div class="content" id="post-content-2288452">
									

<p>1) I plead the 5th.</p>
<p>2) It developed. I initially didn't like it, to be honest. I was a bit of a grouchy gus when I was younger. The love didn't develop until around junior year of high school. I took my first physics class, and realised it was pretty damned cool. That we can so accurately describe the most fundamental constituents of the universe and how they interact is still an endless source of fascination for me. But I am still growing, so, you know, ask me in two years if I don't flop out!</p>
<p>3) Yes, kaktus is a butt, but he's a great butt. Like, 9/10<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-622444-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-622444-1')">1</a></sup></p>
<p>4) Hm&#8230; I don't really have a favourite GOI. I really liked Adventures in Capitalism, but I hold no undue love to Wondertainment itself. I want to like Alexylva, but there's nothing interesting, SCPwise. I do have a least favourite though, and it's the Serpent's Hand. They do have potential, but that's why I dislike them - they're almost universally written the same, as cool wizard people who fight for good and are cool and better than the Foundation. And to me, that's boring and disingenuous to what they're about. There's so much more to them!</p>
