<p>oh wow I forgot this thread existed!</p>
<p>It's good to be back, thank you! As silly as it sounds, I don't think I have one! I do love Set Theory, or maybe alot of Group Theory / Linear Algebra. There were a lot of really cool things I learned in QM that made me think &quot;wow, symmetry is dope&quot;.</p>
<p>No way! Liberal Arts are tough! The thing I like about physics is that there <em>is</em> a right answer. And most of the time there's only one right answer, which makes my life so much easier. But liberal arts, where you need to rely on talent and creativity and ingenuity? That's tough! And I have mad respect for those who make it work.</p>

