<p>Let me tell you something silly in return. I love mathematics but hate being taught it, so I'm always pretty average at it haha.</p>
<p>But I mean, at a certain point, liberal arts becomes very common sense. Of course, there will be debates and stuff but all those moral, ethical, hypothetical dilemmas only really occur in a classroom setting. As you said, the answer is ambiguous! Since there's no right answer, take any route and you'll end up at the final destination anyways (unless you're talking about history and geography, those are hell to memorise)! As someone who's interested in taking up liberal arts in university, I admire the STEM side of stuff more but I'll take the easy way out, thank you. :P</p>

